#== News
#I received a [https://sloan.org/fellowships/2019-Fellows 2019 Sloan Research Fellowship] in Computer Science.








== About Me
I am an associate professor of [http://ece.princeton.edu/ Electrical and Computer Engineering] and [https://www.cs.princeton.edu/ Computer Science] (secondary) in Princeton University and a member of the [https://mltheory.cs.princeton.edu/ Theoretical Machine Learning Group]. Previously, I was a member of the [https://www.math.ias.edu/sp/Optimization_Statistics_and_Theoretical_Machine_Learning IAS] and an assistant professor at USC for three years. Before that, I was a postdoc in the Computer Science Department at UC Berkeley working with [http://www.cs.berkeley.edu/~jordan/ Michael I. Jordan], and also collaborated with [http://people.eecs.berkeley.edu/~brecht/ Ben Recht]. I received my PhD in [https://icme.stanford.edu/ Applied Math] advised by [http://www.stanford.edu/~hastie Trevor Hastie] and [http://statweb.stanford.edu/~jtaylo/ Jonathan Taylor]. I received a BS in Mathematics from Duke University advised by [http://www.math.duke.edu/~mauro/ Mauro Maggioni].
I am a native of Cupertino, CA.\n



My research interests are broadly in
- Foundations of Deep Learning [slides/beyond_ntk.pdf (slides)] [https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vQsuF21tGQk&t=26s (video)]\n
- Representation Learning [slides/representation_learning_slides.pdf Slides] and  [https://www.bilibili.com/video/BV1BA411E7t8?from=search&seid=15450836602360104202 Video].\n
- Foundations of Deep Reinforcement Learning [http://statisticalml.stat.columbia.edu/wp-content/uploads/2019/11/pg_tutorial.pdf (slides)] [https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VRXRocjsR0E (video 1)] [https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZHhzyCwUE1A (video 2)] \n

~~~
{Students, Visitors, and Postdocs}
*Princeton PhD students* interested in machine learning, statistics, or optimization research, please contact me. Any email from prospective students/postdoc/intern, please include the string "filter_student" in the subject, else I will not receive your email. I advise students in Computer Science, Electrical Engineering, Math, ORFE, and PACM. I am recruiting *PhD students* and *postdoctoral scholars* starting in 2023 at Princeton University, please email me a CV apply.  \n

My current focus is on machine learning with a focus on foundations of deep learning, representation learning, and deep reinforcement learning. I have lectured on the Foudations of Deep Learning at MIT [https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vtsjtB6RamE&t=3s Video] and [slides/foundations_DL.pdf Slides]; my tutorial at the Simons Institute:  [slides/simons_tutorial_Overparam_opt_DL.pdf  Slides] and [https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=uC2IGoTE2u4&t=1162s Video]; and my tutorial at Machine Learning Summer School (MLSS 2021): [https://youtu.be/ukxzDErn06E Video] and [slides/beyond_ntk.pdf  Slides].

I have also given tutorials on Representation Learning at the Johns Hopkins Winter School and Beijing AI Institute; [slides/representation_learning_slides.pdf Slides] and  [https://www.bilibili.com/video/BV1BA411E7t8?from=search&seid=15450836602360104202 Video]. 


I am also happy to host *remote visitors*. Summer visitors please contact me around February to schedule your visit. See a list of past visitors at [group.html here].
~~~

